   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The volume of water in a tank is \\( V(t) = 2 t^{2} + t \\) liters at time t minutes. Compute the average rate of change of V over each of the intervals \\( [2, 2.100] \\), \\( [2, 2.010] \\), \\( [2, 2.001] \\), and use them to find the rate at which V is changing at \\( t = 2 \\). Indicate units of measure.",
      "command_verb": "estimate"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 9,
      "units": "liters per minute"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The average rate over \\( [2, 2 + h] \\) is \\( \\frac{V(2 + h) - V(2)}{h} \\), which for h = 0.1, 0.01 and 0.001 gives 9.200, 9.020, 9.002.",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As the intervals shrink the averages approach 9, so the instantaneous rate at \\( t = 2 \\) is 9 liters per minute. Each average is only an approximation of it.",
         "mathjson": 9,
         "rule_named": "instantaneous rate as the limit of average rates"
      }
   ],
